meta {
  name: confirm email link
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/registration/account-confirm-email/:key/
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  key: PASTE_KEY_FROM_THE_EMAIL_LINK
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Not an API call -- this is the URL allauth reverses when building the
  activation link, and it must exist or `send_email_confirmation()` raises and
  no signup email is sent at all.

  `AccountAdapter` rewrites the link in the actual email to
  `{{frontend_url}}/auth/email/confirm/<key>`, so a user should never reach this
  route. If one does (an old link, a client that stripped the rewrite), it 302s
  to that same frontend page rather than 404ing.

  The frontend then posts the key to
  `POST /student/registration/verify-email/`.

  ## API example response
  302 Location: {{frontend_url}}/auth/email/confirm/<key>
}
